jobs.description:
Glovo is part of the Delivery Hero Group, the world’s pioneering local delivery platform, our mission is to deliver an amazing experience—fast, easy, and to your door. We operate in around 70 countries worldwide. Headquartered in Berlin, Germany. Delivery Hero has been listed on the Frankfurt Stock Exchange since 2017 and is part of the MDAX stock market index.

YOUR MISSION

Are you looking for a challenging experience in one of the fastest growing Startups in Europe? Do you want to contribute to building a product that will disrupt the On demand market? If your answer is YES and you are eager to join a strongly data-driven and results-focused team we are looking forward to meeting you! In this role, you will strengthen commercial teams' ability to navigate through data, enabling them to make actionable data-driven decisions!

THE JOURNEY

- Generate and maintain comprehensive internal reports and dashboards for the commercial team to monitor and identify opportunities for our partners;

- Act as a commercial business partner and advisor for the commercial team on data related to promos and ads. This means accessing and processing the data in a way that answers those needs;

- Present results in a well-structured, efficient, and clear manner;

- Ensure high data quality standards by maintaining accuracy and consistency across internal dashboards;

- continuously provide recommendations on existing and new metric definitions to ensure our teams can easily use and find value in the data we provide;

- Monitor daily, weekly, monthly KPIs and landscape and collect relevant insights to help the commercial teams to deliver the country's commercial strategy;

- Prepare ad-hoc reports and draw conclusions related to profitability, orders, active promotions etc. based on stakeholder requests;

- Standardize processes and reporting for enhanced efficiency.

foodpanda is part of the Delivery Hero Group, the world’s pioneering local delivery platform, our mission is to deliver an amazing experience—fast, easy, and to your door. We operate in around 65 countries worldwide. Headquartered in Berlin, Germany. Delivery Hero has been listed on the Frankfurt Stock Exchange since 2017 and is part of the MDAX stock market index.

As the leader of our Local Shops vertical, you will own the end-to-end business across our three brands (foodpanda, foodora and yemeksepeti) spanning Asia, Europe and Turkey. Local Shops is our partner-powered quick commerce business, where we bring the assortment of the region’s leading retailers to customers in minutes. You will set the strategy, own the commercial agenda with our retail partners, and be accountable for the operational quality that turns a partnership into a great customer experience. You will lead a regional team across commercial and operations, and work hand in hand with country teams to grow the vertical aggressively.

Key Responsibilities:

- Own the vertical strategy and roadmap: define where we play (grocery today; health & beauty, DIY, pet and further verticals next), how we win, and the KPI framework and portfolio of initiatives to get there;

- Be accountable for the growth and unit economics of the vertical, steering performance through clear business reviews and disciplined prioritisation of resources;

- Develop and own senior relationships with our regional strategic retail partners: shaping joint business plans, commercial terms, assortment, pricing and monetisation;

- Guide country commercial teams in their sales agenda, account management, category management and monetisation topics, raising the bar on execution across all markets;

- Own operational excellence end to end: partner store execution (availability, picking quality, substitutions, stock accuracy), handover to riders, delivery performance, and the customer experience metrics that follow;

- Build the playbooks, tooling requirements and best practices that let every country execute consistently, acting as the bridge between regional strategy and local reality;

- Lead, structure and develop a regional team spanning commercial and operations, fostering collaboration, learning and high performance;

- Work cross-functionally with product, data, logistics, marketing and finance to co-create the solutions the vertical needs to scale;

- Provide senior management with regular updates on vertical performance, partner developments and market insights.

jobs.requirements_raw:
